# 1️⃣ LEAD & LAG

These are **window functions**.

They help compare rows with:

* previous row
* next row

Without self joins.

---

# 🔹 LAG()

## Big Idea

Gets value from PREVIOUS row.

---

## Mental Model 🧠

```text id="b8cbhr"
LAG = look behind
```

---

# Example Table

| month | sales |
| ----- | ----- |
| Jan   | 100   |
| Feb   | 150   |
| Mar   | 120   |

---

# SQL Query

```sql id="yc7o2q"
SELECT month,
sales,
LAG(sales) OVER (ORDER BY month) AS prev_sales
FROM sales_data;
```

---

# Output

| month | sales | prev_sales |
| ----- | ----- | ---------- |
| Jan   | 100   | NULL       |
| Feb   | 150   | 100        |
| Mar   | 120   | 150        |

---

## Why Useful

Can compare:

```text id="z1q5xv"
Current month vs previous month
```

---

# 🔹 LEAD()

## Big Idea

Gets value from NEXT row.

---

## Mental Model 🧠

```text id="d7h6ig"
LEAD = look ahead
```

---

# Query

```sql id="gn07l1"
SELECT month,
sales,
LEAD(sales) OVER (ORDER BY month) AS next_sales
FROM sales_data;
```

---

# Output

| month | sales | next_sales |
| ----- | ----- | ---------- |
| Jan   | 100   | 150        |
| Feb   | 150   | 120        |
| Mar   | 120   | NULL       |

---

# Python Analogy 🧠

```python id="lg2f0y"
for i in range(len(data)):

    prev_val = data[i-1] if i > 0 else None

    next_val = data[i+1] if i < len(data)-1 else None
```

---

# Why LEAD/LAG Are Powerful

Used for:

* Trend analysis
* Growth calculation
* Time-series analytics

---

# Memory Trick 🧠

```text id="m0h96u"
LAG → previous

LEAD → next
```

